      redefine it. What is local is only the placement and the vocabulary the guarantee wears here:
      a projection-reconcile / stamp path uses `StampMode::{Declare, HealCanonical, GapFill}`.
      `Declare` is ONLY for deliberate canonical channels (declare route, propagation POST,
      own-conductor `ContentHeadDeclared` signal — request-borne/own-authored, may move a head
      anywhere including a deliberate revert); a heal with a canonical answer (`canonical == true`)
      MUST stamp `HealCanonical` — fill, same-head refresh, or a move ONLY with proof of forward
      ordering (`declared_at` newer than the stored `declared_head_at`; NULL either side = refuse —
      that refusal IS C2's "missing ordering evidence refuses the move rather than guessing"); a
      fallback resolve (`canonical == false`, e.g. a cold conductor's root-author election) MUST
      stamp `GapFill` — fill an empty row only. Do not widen `Declare`, and do not key the guard on
